symmetry-requirement-d8d607ad.interpretation:
In this scalar one-generation approximation, $m_{
u}$ represents the effective physical mass of the light active neutrino. The Dirac mass term $m_D = y_{
u} v / \sqrt{2}$ arises from Yukawa coupling $y_{
u}$ with the Higgs vacuum expectation value $v \approx 246	ext{ GeV}$. The denominator $M_R$ is the explicit lepton-number-violating Majorana mass of the right-handed neutrino singlet. Because $M_R \sim 10^{14}	ext{ GeV}$ near the GUT scale, $m_{
u}$ naturally falls in the sub-electronvolt regime without requiring an unnaturally small Yukawa coupling.

